WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.420
You are awake, and you are here.

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.240
Settle in a safe resting position.

3
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:22.895
This practice offers a quiet path through wakefulness; it cannot promise sleep or replace professional care for ongoing sleep difficulty.

4
00:00:24.595 --> 00:00:27.995
You may stop listening at any time.

5
00:00:32.596 --> 00:00:45.851
If something practical needs attention—pain, temperature, medication, a child, an alarm, or safety—take care of it first.

6
00:00:47.551 --> 00:00:52.596
Meditation does not ask you to ignore a real need.

7
00:01:00.264 --> 00:01:06.124
When you are ready, let the clock remain unchecked if that is workable.

8
00:01:07.824 --> 00:01:12.404
You do not need a number to know that you are awake now.

9
00:01:21.606 --> 00:01:31.846
Feel one broad place where the body meets the bed: the back, one side, the head, or the legs.

10
00:01:33.546 --> 00:01:38.301
Let that contact be more important than measuring the night.

11
00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.370
Notice the room as it is.

12
00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.990
Darkness or dim light.

13
00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.290
Near or distant sound.

14
00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.230
Warm or cool air.

15
00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:10.180
Let orientation replace the sense of being lost in time.

16
00:02:22.449 --> 00:02:24.209
Feel an ordinary breath.

17
00:02:25.909 --> 00:02:27.989
Do not deepen or slow it.

18
00:02:29.689 --> 00:02:36.419
Follow only the exhale, then let attention return to the body's weight.

19
00:02:48.688 --> 00:02:54.248
If the mind says you must sleep now, recognize urgency.

20
00:02:55.948 --> 00:03:05.628
The thought is understandable, and you do not have to carry out its demand in this breath.

21
00:03:17.896 --> 00:03:24.691
Try a quieter sentence: for now, I can rest while awake.

22
00:03:26.391 --> 00:03:32.851
You do not need to like wakefulness or choose it for the sentence to be true.

23
00:03:46.654 --> 00:03:49.374
Bring attention to the forehead and eyes.

24
00:03:51.074 --> 00:03:55.839
Notice whether they are searching, focusing, or trying.

25
00:03:57.539 --> 00:04:01.669
Let them receive darkness without looking for sleep.

26
00:04:13.938 --> 00:04:17.488
Feel the jaw, tongue, and throat.

27
00:04:19.188 --> 00:04:23.328
If effort can reduce slightly, allow it.

28
00:04:25.028 --> 00:04:28.898
If it remains, simply know where it is.

29
00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:43.167
Move to shoulders and arms.

30
00:04:44.867 --> 00:04:49.167
Let the bed or blankets meet their weight.

31
00:04:50.867 --> 00:04:55.357
Hands can rest without holding the night together.

32
00:05:09.159 --> 00:05:10.839
Feel the chest and upper back.

33
00:05:12.539 --> 00:05:17.949
Breathing may be quiet, uneven, shallow, or full.

34
00:05:19.649 --> 00:05:22.129
Let it move without becoming a project.

35
00:05:35.932 --> 00:05:38.412
Notice the belly and lower back.

36
00:05:40.112 --> 00:05:45.662
There may be worry, tension, warmth, or little sensation.

37
00:05:47.362 --> 00:05:52.152
Keep the area within the larger support of the bed.

38
00:06:05.955 --> 00:06:10.305
Feel the pelvis, legs, and feet.

39
00:06:12.005 --> 00:06:19.185
Let attention travel slowly downward, then rest at the heels or toes for several moments.

40
00:06:34.521 --> 00:06:40.341
Sense the whole body as one shape lying in a room at night.

41
00:06:42.041 --> 00:06:47.721
You do not need every region to feel clear or relaxed.

42
00:07:03.057 --> 00:07:05.337
Thoughts may be reviewing tomorrow.

43
00:07:07.037 --> 00:07:08.317
Label planning.

44
00:07:10.017 --> 00:07:12.937
Thoughts may be replaying today.

45
00:07:14.637 --> 00:07:15.837
Label remembering.

46
00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:20.697
Thoughts may calculate consequences.

47
00:07:22.397 --> 00:07:23.757
Label forecasting.

48
00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:44.295
Each time, answer with the same small movement: thought, then bed.

49
00:07:45.995 --> 00:07:50.060
Thought, then sound.

50
00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:56.890
Let repetition make the response simpler rather than more forceful.

51
00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:26.919
If a useful idea appears, trust that you can address it after waking, or use the note-taking approach that is already part of your sleep routine.

52
00:08:28.619 --> 00:08:35.179
Do not build a new plan in bed now.

53
00:08:48.982 --> 00:08:53.112
Listen for the farthest sound you can hear.

54
00:08:54.812 --> 00:08:56.492
Then the nearest.

55
00:08:58.192 --> 00:09:02.967
Then let all sounds share one field without ranking them.

56
00:09:18.303 --> 00:09:20.743
Notice the quiet after a sound ends.

57
00:09:22.443 --> 00:09:24.523
Quiet does not have to be complete.

58
00:09:26.223 --> 00:09:31.828
It can be the space in which another sound appears.

59
00:09:45.631 --> 00:09:47.831
Return to contact beneath the body.

60
00:09:49.531 --> 00:09:51.011
Find the heaviest area.

61
00:09:52.711 --> 00:09:57.801
Let the surface receive its weight without imagining that it must sink.

62
00:10:13.137 --> 00:10:16.657
Find the lightest or least clear area.

63
00:10:18.357 --> 00:10:19.797
Include its uncertainty.

64
00:10:21.497 --> 00:10:23.897
A body scan can have blank places.

65
00:10:37.699 --> 00:10:39.219
Now release the scan.

66
00:10:40.919 --> 00:10:45.829
Let awareness become broad, soft, and imprecise.

67
00:10:47.529 --> 00:10:54.309
The body continues to breathe and the bed continues to support it without detailed attention.

68
00:11:12.713 --> 00:11:15.633
Perhaps images or fragments begin to drift.

69
00:11:17.333 --> 00:11:21.648
Do not check whether they mean sleep is close.

70
00:11:23.348 --> 00:11:26.508
Let them form and dissolve without following.

71
00:11:43.378 --> 00:11:45.378
Perhaps the mind remains sharp.

72
00:11:47.078 --> 00:11:52.313
Let sharpness be present inside a body that is resting.

73
00:11:54.013 --> 00:11:58.863
Wakefulness is not an action you must keep performing.

74
00:12:15.732 --> 00:12:20.797
Try counting only exhales from one to five, lightly.

75
00:12:22.497 --> 00:12:23.337
One.

76
00:12:25.037 --> 00:12:29.102
Then the next exhale, two.

77
00:12:30.802 --> 00:12:36.777
If you lose the count, begin at one without evaluating.

78
00:12:59.782 --> 00:13:05.272
Let counting go after five or whenever it becomes work.

79
00:13:06.972 --> 00:13:09.052
Rest with the uncounted rhythm.

80
00:13:27.455 --> 00:13:32.345
If frustration appears, locate one physical trace of it.

81
00:13:34.045 --> 00:13:38.605
Pressure, heat, tightness, movement.

82
00:13:40.305 --> 00:13:45.940
Notice a small area, then return to a larger neutral contact point.

83
00:14:01.276 --> 00:14:08.001
Say quietly: frustration is here; the bed is also here.

84
00:14:09.701 --> 00:14:12.221
Keep both facts in the same moment.

85
00:14:27.558 --> 00:14:29.998
You may choose to change position.

86
00:14:31.698 --> 00:14:38.002
Move slowly, settle blankets again, and feel the new contact map.

87
00:14:39.702 --> 00:14:42.742
A deliberate adjustment is not starting over.

88
00:14:56.545 --> 00:14:59.105
Let the next minute contain no method.

89
00:15:00.805 --> 00:15:05.290
No counting, labeling, scanning, or trying.

90
00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:09.470
Instructions will pause while the night continues.

91
00:15:30.941 --> 00:15:35.571
If you are still listening, notice one exhale.

92
00:15:37.271 --> 00:15:43.451
Then feel both hands or both feet, wherever they rest.

93
00:15:57.253 --> 00:16:07.863
Bring to mind a plain, non-demanding place: a familiar room, a quiet path, a simple patch of sky.

94
00:16:09.563 --> 00:16:11.323
Do not make a vivid story.

95
00:16:13.023 --> 00:16:15.943
Let the image remain incomplete and still.

96
00:16:32.813 --> 00:16:38.753
Notice one neutral detail of that place, then let it fade.

97
00:16:40.453 --> 00:16:44.598
Return to darkness, sound, and weight.

98
00:16:59.934 --> 00:17:02.294
Sleep may arrive without a clear boundary.

99
00:17:03.994 --> 00:17:09.789
If attention becomes scattered or the words stop making sense, allow that.

100
00:17:11.489 --> 00:17:16.164
You do not need to come back to the instruction.

101
00:17:34.568 --> 00:17:41.148
If sleep does not arrive, the practice remains a period of reduced struggle.

102
00:17:42.848 --> 00:17:47.208
Rest has value without being used as a guarantee.

103
00:18:04.078 --> 00:18:07.198
Feel the whole resting shape once more.

104
00:18:08.898 --> 00:18:16.078
Let the forehead be as it is, the breath be as it is, and the night be unfinished.

105
00:18:34.481 --> 00:18:38.726
Release the wish to know what happens next.

106
00:18:40.426 --> 00:18:44.591
For this moment, nothing needs to be decided.

107
00:19:02.994 --> 00:19:04.914
You can stop listening now.

108
00:19:06.614 --> 00:19:18.169
Let the remaining silence belong to sleep if sleep comes, and to quiet wakefulness if it does not.

109
00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:50.360
If you later choose to leave the bed or follow another step in your established sleep-care plan, do so gently and safely.

110
00:19:52.060 --> 00:20:00.000
Until then, let the bed carry the body through this one unhurried moment.
